    "dwarf": {
      "word": "DWARF",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "An animal or plant which is much below the ordinary size of its species or kind; especially, a diminutive human being. of courts and the nobility. the usual or normal size; as, dwarf tree; dwarf honeysuckle. Dwarf elder (Bot.), danewort. building, often used as a garden wall or fence. Gwilt.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To hinder from growing to the natural size; to make or keep small; to stunt. Addison. Even the most common moral ideas and affections . . . would be stunted and dwarfed, if cut off from a spiritual background. J. C. Shairp.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To become small; to diminish in size. Strange power of the world that, the moment we enter it, our great conceptions dwarf. Beaconsfield.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
